        {
          "id": 2522858645,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "After considering it, I think it makes more sense to handle the common case better and revert to the behavior of the Protocol column that was done for roughly five years. The gQUIC dissector could set the Protocol column if it wanted. (Is/was it possible for gQUIC to send more than one HTTP/2 frame/PDU in a single gQUIC frame? If so, arguably it should be calling a different function or calling the PDU function more than once.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
