      "id": "44d5f584524cf43b9f1a87df7f3256b4953f2f9f",
      "short_id": "44d5f584",
      "created_at": "2025-05-24T06:49:33.000+02:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "688c8b0d39a2a782e3692bb2c757837d86c45c54"
      ],
      "title": "HTTP/2: Only set COL_PROTOCOL once",
      "message": "HTTP/2: Only set COL_PROTOCOL once\n\nHTTP/2 DATA frames can call other dissectors which set (or append) to\nCOL_PROTOCOL. Other HTTP/2 frames do not. A packet might have multiple\nHTTP/2 frames, and a DATA frame can be present without being either\nthe first or last HTTP/2 frame. Preferably, COL_PROTOCOL should be\nthe value from a DATA frame.\n\nSince there might be a DATA frame followed by a non-DATA frame, we\ndon't want to set the Protocol column to \"HTTP2\" for each frame (PDU),\nonly for the first. Unfortunately, tcp_dissect_pdus doesn't make that\neasy (it doesn't call a dissector / add a layer for each PDU, so we\ndon't know if we're on the first PDU), so just set it before calling\ntcp_dissect_pdus. Note this does have the effect of setting the column\nto \"HTTP2\" on the first pass for frames that don't dissect any bytes\nand require desegmentation.\n\nPerhaps tcp_dissect_pdus itself should set the Protocol column before\nthe first PDU, either to a string passed in or the protocol short name.\nAlternatively, perhaps HTTP/2 should have its own PDU dissecting\nfunction.\n\nSince the first frame might be a non-DATA frame followed by a DATA\nframe, we don't want to set the Protocol column unwriteable after the\nfirst PDU (e.g., in tcp_dissect_pdus or elsewhere) either.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-05-13T07:23:42.000-04:00",
